 to beat it with a higher pair if they can.  \n2. If they pass, my teammate can take control.  \n3. If they beat it, I still have ♣K high and ♦8, which could win later if my teammate helps.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nIn this late game with the landlord down to 2 cards, playing a pair is stronger than a single because it’s harder to beat if the landlord doesn’t have a higher pair. My teammate might have a high pair or a bomb, but since I don’t know, I should play my strongest combination now to try to win the trick and keep the initiative.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♥9", "♦9"]}'}
